{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_12","type":"agent_message","text":"Fixed the rejected-promise cache poisoning incident.\n\n- Root cause: a rejected origin-load promise remained in the tenant map, so every later read replayed the original timeout as a cache hit. The healthy probe bypassed this in-process cache.\n- Repair: [config-cache.mjs](/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-12pNPr/checkout/benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/config-cache.mjs:47) now removes a failed/invalid load only if it is still the current entry, protecting newer replacements.\n- Regression evidence: [student-tests.mjs](/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-12pNPr/checkout/benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/student-tests.mjs:6) adds three tests covering shared failures and retry, late-failure replacement safety, invalid data, tenant isolation, and successful-cache retention.\n- Incident report: [INCIDENT.md](/private/var/folders/cs/y_h_9x9j2hj316xhs3mvszd80000gn/T/coding-assistant-benchmark-12pNPr/checkout/benchmark/fixtures/T6-rejected-promise-cache/INCIDENT.md:1) documents impact, evidence, misleading signals, repair, coverage, and operating limits.\n- `config-api.mjs`, committed tests, and `incident.log` were unchanged.\n\nVerification: required suite passed, 8/8 tests. `git diff --check` also passed. The optional repository validator could not complete because this checkout lacks the unrelated private T2 test suite.\n\nRemaining concern: successful cache entries still have no expiry or size bound and depend on explicit invalidation, preserving the existing contract."}}
